remain exact **document v0.1 prepublication review drafts** for reference.
Their statement that the full-course download is unpublished describes the
review-time state and is outdated after this prerelease. This README and
current setup page govern availability. The PDF has not been revised or
reissued; see the [publication notice](teaching/phys3810-fa2026/handouts/PUBLICATION_NOTICE.md).

This code prerelease is distinct from the unchanged Grover-only code rc1 and
its document-v0.2 guides. The student PDF is included inside this ZIP; it is
not offered as a separately updated PDF release asset.

## Scope and remaining decisions

The lessons cover Grover on 2–5 qubits; exact QFT on 1–6 qubits; QPE with 1–6
counting qubits and one/two targets; exact-spectrum positive-Hermitian 2x2 HHL;
and a compiled full-domain N=15 Shor example with four residue qubits. These
are small instructional examples, without claims of general scalability or
quantum advantage.

Only the documented Ubuntu/Linux path has execution evidence. Native Windows
x64, macOS ARM64/Intel, native editor UI, and human classroom pacing remain
untested. Windows ARM64 and 32-bit Python are outside the stated target.
Teaching, platform, delivery, and assessment decisions remain pending.

Instructor guides, instructor PDFs, and presenter answer sheets are excluded.
The notebooks, mathematical contracts, and tests still contain worked results
and expected answers. This is **not an answer-free assessment package**; follow
the instructor's eventual collaboration, solution, and submission directions.

## File identity

[MANIFEST.json](MANIFEST.json) records the source revision, both builder hashes,
file hashes, modes, expected validation counts, and disclosed document adaptations.
Runtime source, tests, eight notebooks, dependencies, license, lint configuration,
and both reviewed student-guide files retain exact committed bytes. Technical
contracts retain their mathematical/API/acceptance bodies; repository status
and history framing is omitted. Current setup preserves all six reviewed
fenced blocks and all instructions after the introductory availability paragraph.

There are 47 payload files plus the manifest. Environments, credentials, Git
metadata, generated execution outputs, prompts, policy/chat records, old
archives, and instructor answer documents are excluded. The manifest excludes
itself; the separate release checksum identifies the complete ZIP.
